<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">German Palatines</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palatines were German emigrants from the Electoral Palatinate and neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> territories who left in large numbers in the eighteenth century, driven by war, poverty and religious pressure. About 13,000 reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1709, and many were settled in the Hudson valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, in Ireland and in North Carolina. Later waves went mostly to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, where they formed a large part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania-dutch">Pennsylvania Dutch</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-palatines.jpg" alt="German Palatines" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Skipper Michael at Palatine German Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wabbe_Rhoipalz_-_Feld.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
